hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24378","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt narrated to me, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Hadrad, from his father Abdullah ibn Abi Hadrad, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us to Idam, so I went out among a group of Muslims, among them Abu Qatadah al-Harith ibn Rib'i and Muhallam ibn Jaththamah ibn Qays, and we went out until when we were at the belly of Idam, Amir al-Ashja'i passed by us on a young camel of his with a milk-skin, and when he passed by us he greeted us, so we held back from him, and Muhallam ibn Jaththamah attacked him and killed him due to something that had been between him and him, and took his camel and his goods, then when we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him the news, there was revealed concerning us the Quran: O you who believe, when you go forth in the cause of Allah, verify, and do not say to whoever casts peace to you: You are not a believer, seeking the goods of worldly life, for with Allah are abundant spoils, thus you were before, and Allah favored you, so verify, Allah is aware of what you do."
"24379","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Ja'far, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Abi Awn, from his grandmother, from Ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, that he mentioned that he married a woman, so he came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seeking his help for her dowry, so he said: How much did you give as dowry, he said: I said: Two hundred dirhams, he said: Had you been scooping dirhams from this valley of yours, you would not have increased, I have nothing to give you, so I stayed, then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called me and sent me in an expedition he sent toward Najd, and said: Go out in this expedition, perhaps you may gain something and I shall give it to you as extra, so we went out until we came to the settlement in the evening, and when the darkness of dinner passed, our commander sent us two by two, and we surrounded the camp, and said: When I say takbir and charge, say takbir and charge, and said when he sent us two by two: Do not separate, and I shall ask one of you about the news of his companion and not find him with him, and do not go deep in pursuit, and when we wanted to charge, I heard a man of the settlement shout: O Khadrah, so I took it as a good omen that we would gain greenery from them, and when night darkened, our commander said takbir and charged, and we said takbir and charged, and a man with a sword in his hand passed by me, so I followed him, and my companion said to me: Our commander has covenanted to us not to go deep in pursuit, so return, and when I saw naught but to follow him, he said: By Allah you shall return, or I shall return to him and tell him you refused, so I said: By Allah I shall follow him, so I followed him until when I drew near him, I shot him with an arrow on the ridge of his back, and he fell and said: Come, O Muslim, to Paradise, and when he saw me not drawing near him, and I shot him with another arrow and wounded him deeply, he threw the sword at me and missed me, and I took the sword and killed him and cut off his head with it, and we drove many camels and sheep, then we left, and in the morning my camel was tied to a camel with a beautiful young woman, and she kept turning behind her and saying takbir, so I said to her: Where are you turning to, she said: To a man, by Allah if he is alive he has mingled with you, I said: And I thought he was my companion whom I killed, by Allah I had killed him, and this is his sword hung on the saddle of the camel I am on, and the sword sheath with nothing in it hung on the saddle of her camel, and when I said that to her, she said: Then here is this sheath, sheathe it in it if you are truthful, so I took it and sheathed it in it and it fit it, and when she saw that she wept, then we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he gave me of those camels we came with."
